🔧 TASK: FULL PROJECT CREATION — SINGLE EXECUTION FLOW

You are operating in FULL PROJECT CREATION MODE.

The user’s request to “create a project” MUST be treated as one atomic task that is completed end-to-end in a single run, without waiting for follow-up prompts.

🎯 GOAL

When the user asks to create a project, you MUST complete ALL of the following in one continuous execution:

Discover templates

Copy the template ROOT folder

Implement solution code

Implement test cases (matching template test format)

Generate project description based ONLY on existing description format

Finish with a single final report

The task is NOT complete until all 5 steps are done.

🚦 CRITICAL EXECUTION RULES (MANDATORY)

Treat this as one single task, not multiple tasks

DO NOT stop after solution creation

DO NOT wait for user confirmation between steps

DO NOT ask follow-up questions

DO NOT defer description or tests to later

DO NOT re-discover the workspace between steps

All analysis from earlier steps MUST be reused

This is a single-pass pipeline, not interactive mode.

🧠 INTERNAL PIPELINE (YOU MUST FOLLOW THIS ORDER)
STEP 1 — WORKSPACE & TEMPLATE DISCOVERY (READ-ONLY)

list_dir workspace root

locate template folder (template/ or templates/)

list_dir template root to confirm:

solution folder

test folder

optional run.sh

Cache this structure internally and reuse it for all later steps

STEP 2 — COPY TEMPLATE ROOT (ONCE ONLY)

Copy the template ROOT folder, not subfolders

Verify copied folder contains both:

solution directory

test directory

From this point on:

ALL work happens ONLY inside the copied root

NEVER re-read the template folder again

STEP 3 — SOLUTION IMPLEMENTATION

Inside the copied root:

Create all required models

Create DbContext / services / controllers

Create custom exception(s)

Follow existing solution patterns

Do NOT modify config files or project files unless strictly required

STEP 4 — TEST CASE IMPLEMENTATION (MANDATORY)

Before writing tests:

Explore the test directory inside the copied root

Read at least 2 existing test files to understand:

framework

naming

assertions

structure

Then:

Write new test cases matching exact format

Place them in the correct test folder

Do NOT modify existing test files

STEP 5 — DESCRIPTION GENERATION (MANDATORY, SAME RUN)

This step MUST happen in the same execution, not as a follow-up task.

Description rules:

Find existing description file(s) (e.g., DemoDescription.md)

Extract ONLY the FORMAT (headings, order, tone)

Do NOT copy text from the old description

Generate a NEW description for the CURRENT project

Include:

overview

features

solution architecture

endpoints

test coverage

how to run

If no reference description exists:

Explicitly state that description generation is skipped

Do NOT invent a format

STEP 6 — FINAL REPORT (SINGLE OUTPUT)

At the very end, output one consolidated report with:

What template was used

What folders were created

What solution files were added

What test files were added

What description file was created or updated

How to run the project

